{"id": "EUVD-2026-107256", "enisaUuid": "7fd878d2-a6ba-3e66-9c8e-5f4b1a4ef34d", "description": "A recursive BIND server that receives a query with recursion desired (RD=1) followed by a non-recursive query (RD=0) may exit with an assertion failure, resulting in a denial of service. To be vulnerable, the BIND server must allow recursive queries and have at least two RPZ zones configured: one with the default setting of \"recursive-only yes\", and the other with \"recursive-only no\".\nThis issue affects BIND 9 versions 9.16.0 through 9.18.50, 9.20.0 through 9.20.29, 9.21.0 through 9.21.26, 9.11.3-S1 through 9.18.50-S1, and 9.20.9-S1 through 9.20.29-S1.", "datePublished": "2026-10-21T12:47:28", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T17:19:13", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://kb.isc.org/docs/cve-2026-97313", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.20.30", "https://downloads.isc.org/isc/bind9/9.21.27"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97313", "GHSA-9p2q-wv22-f9q8"], "assigner": "isc", "epss": 0.45, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "10b03ff0-cb73-3637-90f1-123bf83a48e6", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.9-S1 \u22649.20.29-S1"}, {"id": "15fa55b5-2ed0-3205-a53a-99357026241d", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.21.0 \u22649.21.26"}, {"id": "8dec128f-c7df-35a6-8b97-f95481d7199c", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.11.3-S1 \u22649.18.50-S1"}, {"id": "b342f6e4-acb1-3839-a0c7-8251a0a0a699", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.20.0 \u22649.20.29"}, {"id": "e6acf024-acf8-3e34-9f7d-7e09eae79f8d", "product": {"name": "BIND 9", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}, "product_version": "9.16.0 \u22649.18.50"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9cd90ad1-4549-3715-b682-f6ae62a72540", "vendor": {"name": "ISC"}}], "isExploited": false}